      category: "Clubs & Balls",
      allCategories: ["Clubs & Balls"],
      subCategories: ["Clubs"],
      description: "Ben Hogan Golf carries one of the most revered names in golf history, a brand built on the legacy of one of the game's greatest ball-strikers and now focused on precision-engineered clubs sold directly to consumers. The original Ben Hogan Company was founded in 1953 by Hogan himself, producing clubs that emphasized craftsmanship and performance for skilled players. After changing hands several times and fading from prominence, the brand was revived in 2015 by brothers Scott and Terry Koehler, who repositioned it as a direct-to-consumer club company targeting serious golfers who value ball-striking and traditional club design. The modern Ben Hogan Golf focuses on irons, wedges, and now drivers, emphasizing milled faces, precise tolerances, and construction details that appeal to better players and purists. The brand's messaging leans heavily into Hogan's legacy and the idea that technology should serve the swing, not replace skill. Ben Hogan Golf avoids retail distribution, selling exclusively through its website and relying on detailed product information, fitting guides, and a 30-day trial period to convert customers without in-person try-before-you-buy experiences. The company's PTx irons and TK wedges have earned positive reviews from equipment testers and loyal customers who appreciate the brand's focus on traditional shaping and workability. Ben Hogan Golf represents a counterargument to the equipment industry's mass-market, technology-driven approach, instead positioning itself as the choice for golfers who believe ball-striking fundamentals matter more than launch monitors and AI-designed faces. The brand remains small compared to Titleist, Callaway, and TaylorMade, but it has carved out a profitable niche by appealing to a specific type of golfer: one who wants clubs that reward good swings rather than forgive bad ones.",
