      allCategories: ["Tech & Training Aids"],
      subCategories: ["Shafts"],
      description: "FreeFlex represents one of the most unconventional innovations in golf shaft design, producing ultra-flexible shafts engineered to increase clubhead speed and optimize energy transfer through exaggerated bend and release. Founded in 2019 by SJ Golf Engineering Lab and based in Seoul, South Korea, FreeFlex challenges traditional shaft design principles by creating shafts that flex far more than conventional models, creating a pronounced lag and whip effect during the downswing. The brand's shafts are designed to store and release energy more efficiently, theoretically allowing golfers to generate higher clubhead speeds without increasing swing effort. FreeFlex targets players seeking distance gains, particularly those with moderate swing speeds who may benefit from the additional energy transfer. The brand's shafts have gained attention in the fitting community and among club professionals intrigued by the unconventional design, though they remain a niche product compared to major shaft manufacturers like True Temper, KBS, or Graphite Design. FreeFlex's marketing emphasizes measurable speed gains and features testimonials from players who have seen distance improvements after switching. The brand's approach reflects a broader trend in golf equipment toward speed optimization and biomechanical efficiency, as manufacturers seek new ways to help golfers hit the ball farther without requiring physical changes. While FreeFlex has not achieved widespread tour adoption, it has carved out a following among speed-focused amateurs and fitters willing to experiment with non-traditional designs. The brand's success will likely depend on its ability to demonstrate consistent performance across a wide range of players and swing types, as well as its capacity to scale distribution and build credibility in a category dominated by established manufacturers.",
