      category: "Bags & Accessories",
      allCategories: ["Bags & Accessories"],
      subCategories: ["Bags"],
      description: "Jones Sports Co originally launched in 1971 as one of the first brands to produce lightweight carry bags designed specifically for walking golfers. The brand's minimalist nylon bags became iconic in the 1970s and 80s, but the company eventually faded as cart bags and stand bags dominated the market. Jones was revived in the 2010s, re-launching with updated versions of its classic carry bag designs aimed at golfers nostalgic for simpler equipment and the culture of walking the course. The brand's bags feature clean lines, durable construction, and a deliberate lack of excessive pockets, logos, or features that have become standard on modern golf bags. Jones offers pencil bags, Sunday bags, and slim carry bags in solid colors and vintage-inspired designs that appeal to golfers who view their equipment as much about aesthetic as utility. The brand operates primarily direct-to-consumer online but has built a loyal following among minimalist-minded golfers and those drawn to the walking culture that has re-emerged in recent years. Jones positions itself against the trend toward larger, feature-heavy bags designed for carts and push carts, instead celebrating portability and simplicity. The brand has expanded modestly into accessories like headcovers and apparel, but bags remain its core focus. Jones's identity is rooted in nostalgia and a rejection of over-engineered golf equipment—it's not trying to innovate storage technology or add more organizational features, but rather offer an alternative for golfers who want less. The brand's challenge is remaining relevant as the golf bag market continues to segment and as competitors like Vessel and Mackenzie bring more design-forward options to the walking bag category.",
