      allCategories: ["Tech & Training Aids"],
      subCategories: ["Shafts"],
      description: "Oban is a Carlsbad-based premium shaft manufacturer founded in 2007, specializing in high-performance graphite shafts for drivers, fairways, and hybrids. The brand positions itself at the upper end of the shaft market, competing with Japanese stalwarts like Fujikura and Graphite Design by emphasizing precision engineering, consistent manufacturing tolerances, and tour-level performance. Oban shafts are typically found in custom fitting studios and high-end club builds rather than off-the-rack retail offerings, targeting serious players willing to invest in optimized equipment.\n\nOban's product philosophy centers on creating shafts with specific bend profiles, torque characteristics, and weight distributions designed to match particular swing dynamics. The company offers a range of families—including the Kiyoshi, Devotion, and CT series—each engineered for different swing speeds, tempos, and delivery patterns. Oban emphasizes feel and feedback, qualities often prioritized by better players who can discern subtle differences in shaft behavior. The brand has cultivated a loyal following among club fitters and tour players seeking alternatives to mass-market options, though it maintains a relatively low public profile compared to brands with extensive tour marketing.\n\nOban's reputation is built largely on word-of-mouth within the fitting community and among discerning amateurs who prioritize performance over brand recognition. The company doesn't chase widespread tour counts or flashy endorsements; instead, it focuses on producing shafts that perform consistently and meet exacting specifications. This approach appeals to players who view shaft selection as critical to optimizing launch conditions and dispersion, and who are willing to pay premium prices—often several hundred dollars per shaft—for that precision. In an industry where shaft technology can seem opaque and marketing-driven, Oban represents a more engineering-focused ethos, earning credibility through performance rather than hype.",
