      allCategories: ["Apparel & Footwear"],
      subCategories: ["Shoes", "Luxury/High-End"],
      description: "OluKai, founded in 2005 and headquartered in Irvine, California, is a premium footwear brand rooted in Hawaiian craftsmanship, comfort, and island-inspired design. While not exclusively a golf brand, OluKai has cultivated a dedicated following among golfers drawn to its laid-back aesthetic and emphasis on all-day wearability. The brand's name translates to \"my island\" in Hawaiian, and its design philosophy reflects a blend of coastal lifestyle and functional craftsmanship, using premium leathers, anatomical footbeds, and construction techniques that prioritize long-term comfort.\n\nOluKai's entry into golf comes primarily through its casual slip-on styles and leather shoes that golfers wear off the course or in resort settings where relaxed dress codes prevail. Models like the Nohea Moku and the 'Ohana sandals have become staples in warm-weather golf destinations, appealing to players who value comfort and versatility over traditional golf footwear. While OluKai doesn't produce spiked golf shoes or performance-oriented designs, its footwear has found traction in the post-round clubhouse, beach golf settings, and among players seeking stylish alternatives to sneakers or boat shoes.\n\nThe brand's reputation is built on quality materials—full-grain leather, breathable mesh, and durable rubber outsoles—and a commitment to craftsmanship that resonates with golfers who appreciate thoughtful design and premium construction. OluKai positions itself in the lifestyle category, overlapping with brands like Peter Millar and Johnnie-O that blend golf culture with broader coastal or resort aesthetics. Its presence in golf is less about performance metrics and more about cultural fit—appealing to players who embrace a relaxed, island-inspired approach to the game and who prioritize comfort and style in their off-course footwear choices.",
