      description: "Project X revolutionized golf shaft design when it launched in 1992, introducing steel shafts specifically engineered for aggressive swing speeds and tour-level ball-striking. Manufactured by True Temper Sports in Memphis, Tennessee, Project X shafts challenged the prevailing wisdom that lighter meant better, instead offering heavier, stiffer profiles that delivered tighter dispersion and increased control for players who could handle the additional weight. The original Project X steel shaft became ubiquitous on professional tours, trusted by players who prioritized consistency and workability over distance gains. The brand expanded into graphite with the HZRDUS line, targeting driver and fairway wood applications where weight savings matter more than in irons. Project X HZRDUS shafts quickly gained tour adoption, with distinct color-coded models (Black, Red, Smoke) indicating different launch and spin characteristics. The brand's success stems from its focus on custom fitting and precise performance attributes rather than one-size-fits-all solutions. Club fitters trust Project X because its shafts deliver predictable results across a range of swing types, making them essential components in premium custom builds. While recreational golfers may not notice differences between shaft brands, better players and professionals recognize Project X as a performance standard. The brand maintains strong relationships with tour players and equipment manufacturers, serving as an OEM shaft option for numerous club brands while also selling directly through custom fitting channels. In an equipment category often dominated by marginal gains and marketing claims, Project X built credibility through measurable performance improvements and endorsement from players whose livelihoods depend on consistency. The brand represents the engineering-focused approach to golf equipment, where reputation is earned through results rather than advertising.",
